  <page_number>47</page_number>
  <running_head>LYRICA.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <p><i>Franciscus ex quo mollia turpiter</i></p>
    <p><i>Euertit audax otia Guisius,</i></p>
    <p><i>Bellique ciuilis sceleftus</i></p>
    <p><i>Francigenas violauit author,</i></p>
    <p><i>Regnique spretis ordinibus ferox</i></p>
    <p><i>Edicta princeps regia subruit,</i></p>
    <p><i>Cum matre cogens, heu! tenellum</i></p>
    <p><i>Armasequi miseranda Regem:</i></p>
    <p><i>O quàm superbo sœuit impetu!</i></p>
    <p><i>O quanta Gallis damna tulit furens?</i></p>
    <p><i>Quantosque funestus per vrbes</i></p>
    <p><i>Francigenas dedit ille motus!</i></p>
    <p><i>Sic quum quietos diluuies fera</i></p>
    <p><i>Irritat amnes, &amp; pecus &amp; domos,</i></p>
    <p><i>Stirpesque raptas voluit una,</i></p>
    <p><i>Murmure cuncta fremunt tremendo.</i></p>
    <p><i>Sic inquieto nubilus Adria</i></p>
    <p><i>Tollit procellas Africus horridas:</i></p>
    <p><i>Nautasque per vastum vagantes</i></p>
    <p><i>Exagitat violentus æquor.</i></p>
    <p><i>Sic dira sœuit bellua, quum fames</i></p>
    <p><i>Vasana torquet, dentéque feruido</i></p>
    <p><i>Irata prædam quum repertam,</i></p>
    <p><i>Lanigerósve greges trucidat.</i></p>
    <p><i>Hinc arua passim Gallica sanguine</i></p>
    <p><i>Madent refuso, prædáque tristibus</i></p>
    <p><i>Feris per agros funeratæ</i></p>
    <p><i>Francigenûm iacuere turmæ.</i></p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Long s rendered as plain s throughout. Some letters in the scan are damaged (for example "Ædicta" in line 6 and "Vasana" in line 22 are uncertain); the reading "Edicta" and "Vasana" is likely but not fully certain. The first word of line 2 "Euertit" and "Guisius" are as printed.</notes>
